1.21.1-fabric: Chunk 2 - bulk vanilla code migration to 1.21 APIs

Cherry-picked entity/item/block/client/util/container source from the
1.21.1 NeoForge branch (which had already navigated the 1.20.1 -> 1.21.1
vanilla MC API changes), then scrubbed NeoForge-specific bits:

- @OnlyIn(Dist.CLIENT) -> @Environment(EnvType.CLIENT)
- net.neoforged.api.distmarker.* imports removed
- net.neoforged.neoforge.* and net.minecraftforge.* imports removed
- canDrownInFluidType / NeoForgeMod.WATER_TYPE -> can_breathe_under_water
  entity_type tag (canBreatheUnderwater is final on LivingEntity in 1.21,
  derived from EntityTypeTags.CAN_BREATHE_UNDER_WATER)
- GeckoLib core.* package paths flattened to 4.7 layout (animation,
  animatable, etc. - core. is gone)
- javax.annotation.Nullable / Nonnull / CheckForNull -> jetbrains
  annotations.Nullable / NotNull (Fabric ships those, not JSR-305)

Restored Fabric-specific config/ tree (CNBConfig + handler) since the
NeoForge versions use org.infernalstudios.config which isn't on the
Fabric classpath; Fabric uses night-config TOML instead.

Restored Fabric-flavored FlowerCrownItem and SporelingBackpackItem
because those use the GeoItem RenderProvider pattern unique to Fabric
GeckoLib (NeoForge uses GeoArmorRenderer.registerFor instead).

Build is still red - 100 source-level errors remain, mostly init/* files
that need DeferredRegister patterns swapped for Fabric Registry calls.
Next chunk will tackle those.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
